# Project Walkthrough: ECG Foundation Representation System

This walkthrough details the development history, model architectures, benchmarking phases, explainability integration, and current unified state of the **ECG Foundation Representation System**.

---

## 1. Project Goal & High-Level Architecture
The primary objective of this project is to build a multi-modal foundation system for 12-lead ECG representation learning. The system is designed to fuse three complementary representations:
1. **Temporal Encoder ($Z_{temporal}$)**: Captures continuous time-series sequence dynamics.
2. **Biomarker Encoder ($Z_{biomarker}$)**: Reconstructs and classifies clinical handcrafted features (HRV, intervals, segment amplitudes).
3. **Morphology Encoder ($Z_{morphology}$)**: Captures beat-level visual shape features (spectrograms, recurrence plots, or GAFs).

The fused representations are eventually passed to a unified classification and downstream clinical prediction engine.

```mermaid
graph TD
    RawECG["Raw 12-Lead ECG Data"] --> Preprocess["Signal Preprocessing Pipeline"]
    
    %% Encoder Layers
    Preprocess --> TemporalEnc["Temporal Encoder (ResNet-SE / Transformer)"]
    Preprocess --> BiomarkerExtract["Clinical Feature Extractor"]
    Preprocess --> MorphologySegment["Beat Segmenter"]
    
    BiomarkerExtract --> BiomarkerEnc["Biomarker Encoder (FT-Transformer Autoencoder)"]
    MorphologySegment --> MorphologyEnc["Morphology Encoder (2D ResNet)"]
    
    %% Embeddings
    TemporalEnc --> Ztemp["Z_temporal (64-dim)"]
    BiomarkerEnc --> Zbio["Z_biomarker (32-dim)"]
    MorphologyEnc --> Zmorph["Z_morphology (512-dim)"]
    
    %% Fusion and Output
    Ztemp & Zbio & Zmorph --> Fusion["Adaptive Fusion Engine"]
    Fusion --> UnifiedClass["Unified Classifier"]
    UnifiedClass --> XAI["Grad-CAM & SHAP Explainability"]
```

